---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavierStokesProofAtlas from "@/components/labs/NavierStokesProofAtlas.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Navier–Stokes proof atlas — bordumb"
  description="An interactive map of the sparse Gaussian certificate, its ranked proof ledger, the active radial-tail decomposition, and the remaining logical distance to the Clay problem."
>
  <article class="atlas-page page-shell">
    <header class="atlas-hero">
      <div class="hero-index" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>NS</span>
        <i></i>
        <small>2026·08·02</small>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Navier–Stokes · formal proof observatory</p>
        <h1>One obstruction,<br /><em>under a microscope.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-deck">
          The agent is converting an explicit Gaussian witness into a global,
          kernel-checked no-go theorem. This atlas shows the exact object under
          analysis, what each commit established, and where the work stops
          short of the Millennium problem.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-boundary">
        <span>Current boundary</span>
        <strong>Twofold-X radial tail</strong>
        <p>
          Two radial coefficients are closed. Five angular slices must erase
          the remaining degree-ten quotient; slice zero is the active bridge.
        </p>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Evidence</dt>
            <dd>Exact rational + Lean kernel</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Conclusion</dt>
            <dd>Closure obstruction only</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <NavierStokesProofAtlas />

    <section class="reading-note" aria-labelledby="reading-note-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How to read the atlas</p>
        <h2 id="reading-note-title">A child theorem does not solve its parent.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-columns">
        <p>
          <strong>Kernel-checked</strong> means Lean accepted the theorem and
          its reported dependencies contain only the standard foundational
          axioms used throughout Mathlib. It does not mean every theorem that
          imports it is complete.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Exact certificate</strong> means rational computation found
          a finite proof object without floating-point theorem data. It becomes
          a formal theorem only after Lean independently checks its generated
          inequalities and the assembly covers the stated domain.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Closure obstruction</strong> means the proposed universal
          estimate cannot hold in its current form. Eliminating that strategy
          narrows the search; it supplies neither a global regularity estimate
          nor a finite-time singular solution.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="atlas-footer">
      <p>
        The companion visual study explains the vorticity geometry that
        motivated the formal program before the Gaussian obstruction emerged.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/labs/vortex-stretching">
        Explore the vortex geometry
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .atlas-page {
    padding-bottom: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
  }

  .atlas-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4rem minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(17rem, 0.38fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: end;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .hero-index {
    display: grid;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 15rem;
    justify-items: center;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .hero-index span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .hero-index i {
    width: 1px;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 8rem;
    background: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .hero-index small {
    align-self: end;
    font-size: 0.52rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
  }

  .hero-copy h1 {
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(3.25rem, 7.5vw, 7rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.063em;
    line-height: 0.88;
  }

  .hero-copy h1 em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .hero-deck {
    max-width: 43rem;
    margin: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.8vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.58;
  }

  .hero-boundary {
    padding: 1.25rem 0 0 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .hero-boundary > span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hero-boundary > strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .hero-boundary > p {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .hero-boundary dl {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-boundary dl div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding-block: 0.55rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .hero-boundary dt {
    color: var(--faint);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hero-boundary dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .reading-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(16rem, 0.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }

  .reading-note h2 {
    max-width: 25rem;
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .reading-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .reading-columns p {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .reading-columns strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .atlas-footer {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }

  .atlas-footer p {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .atlas-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .hero-boundary {
      grid-column: 2;
      border-left: 0;
    }

    .reading-note {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .atlas-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero-index {
      display: none;
    }

    .hero-boundary {
      grid-column: 1;
      padding-left: 0;
    }

    .reading-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .atlas-footer {
      display: grid;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
